  "body": "## Results\n\nThis draft collects three independently audited results for Stanford Question 2.13 (10400035 / AMR-103-0035), in the ordinary unframed smooth ordered fixed-endpoint rational string-link category:\n\n1. The Milnor/free-exterior span fails at (k,n)=(2,2). The intersection with the entire all-length repeated-index Milnor algebra is span_Q{1, linking, linking\u00b2}; the first component Conway coefficient is outside M_2(2)+N_2(2).\n2. N_n(k)=0 for every k\u22652 and 0\u2264n\u22642.\n3. N_7(2) contains a nonzero invariant of exact order seven, hence N_n(2)\u22600 for every n\u22657.\n\nThe third proof includes the complete marked free-reversal lemma, with exact outer-boundary agreement, collar correction, tube filling, and relative-ball isotopy. It then uses the ordinary rational Duzhin\u2013Karev v5 theorem and weight-system integration. The result is existential; no named nonsingular-link numeric value is claimed.\n\n## Evidence and attribution\n\nThe package preserves all authored mathematics in the three full proofs, four supporting lemmas, three independent whole-proof audits, the separate written algebra audit, and two bounded literature/context reviews. Only documented provenance/privacy and unavailable-artifact edits are made. The original source reports are unchanged.\n\nPrincipal established ingredients are Meilhan\u2019s ordinary degree-two classification; repeated-index Milnor concordance invariance; Nogueira\u2019s free tangle; Kauffman\u2013Lambropoulou\u2019s rational-tangle construction; Willerton\u2019s Conway normalization; classical genus-two hyperelliptic extension/centrality; Hatcher\u2019s relative-ball theorem; and Duzhin\u2013Karev\u2019s ordinary unframed rational degree-seven orientation detector. Public citations, exact editions, access limits, and historical inspection records are retained.\n\nThese are AI mathematical audits, not human peer review or formal proof-assistant verification. No novelty or earliest-priority claim is made.\n\n## Theoretical edition and remaining scope\n\nNo executable scripts, fixtures, computational result files, or logs are included. Historical computational passages remain identified as supplementary prior-audit accounts, not checks rerun for this edition. Existing mathematical calculations, including the degree-seven trace polynomial and integer-matrix example, are preserved as authored exposition. No executable check was rewritten into prose to replace an omitted artifact.\n\nOrders three through six on two strands remain unresolved, as do general higher-strand higher-order kernels and general classifications. There is no least-order claim or extension of the order-two spanning failure to all larger orders. The campaign stopped after 3 of 5 approaches; two remain unused and no further approach was spent on packaging.\n\n## Exact file scope\n\nAdd only the nineteen files listed below under unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/10400035/. No QUEUE.md or unrelated file is changed. No copied third-party source body, dataset content, private source, private coordination material, or mixed private artifact inventory is included. SOURCES.json records sixteen public PDF identities locally rechecked for this edition, without source bodies. The noncircular manifest hashes the eighteen other files; its own identity is pinned below.\n\n## File identity pins\n\n- ACCEPTANCE.md: 6,148 bytes; SHA-256 afcc02787fc037eb481bba7796f376cc685bf6e2642466ba42245ead3122039a\n- AUDIT_KERNEL_ORDER_SEVEN.md: 22,119 bytes; SHA-256 b568e0dcadb3b3401b4f346f094b1585abee040f843752d607db47985d3c4e98\n- AUDIT_KERNEL_ORDER_TWO.md: 24,272 bytes; SHA-256 5af08ea7d108151c2f44e9bb5b5e19dcf85e554a5613c719d9359da692aa5467\n- AUDIT_ORDER_TWO_ALGEBRA.md: 8,536 bytes; SHA-256 93ea14e23101ba030e66903d9ba750ed932ce4f1b06594179b322d2ad9837388\n- AUDIT_SPAN_ORDER_TWO.md: 18,999 bytes; SHA-256 c00c1b9057dcd7d67f25b3cbbf5225598f5ae270db8d68ac4a8f057613ff6b02\n- FILTERED_MILNOR_ORDER_TWO_LEMMA.md: 9,665 bytes; SHA-256 68189680279f3dd95a03874442431a98aa78d0467358820c67bd8f8691018073\n- GEOMETRIC_EXISTENCE.md: 11,732 bytes; SHA-256 533c7204552e71ca364162755867bdd356d6cd5aa2a920c6c8bc675d7a87df53\n- MANIFEST.json: 3,678 bytes; SHA-256 9c9d1af69f6121ebb2b2cbb2a1d157f5a9c018da28351b85f2d461626f07240b\n- MARKED_FREE_REVERSAL_LEMMA.md: 13,755 bytes; SHA-256 e82a3d37dcfaf98bafd6fa9afb1e2b6da37904769d1146b553a082698e549db1\n- PRIORITY_REVERSAL_ORDER_SEVEN.md: 10,148 bytes; SHA-256 25c257aa282bfc3601c78b4a5990aa0cb31e05cc79768e9b9b5d9c695bedd890\n- PRIORITY_SPAN_ORDER_TWO.md: 8,624 bytes; SHA-256 a13232b68c1ba2431655996b979ce9e4e68ea7987bc4bb8a2776cade7259ec64\n- PROOF_KERNEL_ORDER_SEVEN.md: 18,873 bytes; SHA-256 1feb22a2e5fc4e3ead78c409d48f7631e05a2d97e4ca7ab1cf07f15c5b2a17b0\n- PROOF_KERNEL_ORDER_TWO.md: 18,434 bytes; SHA-256 46e2c08954f9854c4c267b675b1339055e82963e52e8e8c13f821d3b348b4b6c\n- PROOF_SPAN_ORDER_TWO.md: 16,047 bytes; SHA-256 3775372fba9316c7ec0348110639c87a0720d5ea3aae7f12b1e2f5635e9b6d85\n- PROVENANCE.md: 6,856 bytes; SHA-256 340dcdcae467852d52dc43983ea82538446c680f948c12f6e84f8a09cb082af6\n- RATIONAL_FREE_WITNESS.md: 11,252 bytes; SHA-256 ad0b435e4f4612075e1c0460c5345be9bd9fddde9ecf9c49a30014303c375633\n- README.md: 6,932 bytes; SHA-256 12a78cfaf7a9492c2c84749a15fe47351c26acfcae1ecaade2f102e66df7bfb7\n- SOURCES.json: 20,310 bytes; SHA-256 9b9b52f7aadaa767b44404d122d9f50e79dbc5cb331fc706ba724c322da8c43d\n- STATUS.json: 2,474 bytes; SHA-256 cbb57c3e4bae9ed8604012a7019731235a9c215348fa008480f2d5e17cf10d64\n",
